cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using
  the metadata in this file.

title: >-
  nife: Oral biofilm community dynamics — Hamilton/gLV inference
  with metabolic sign priors and COMETS dFBA

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Nishioka
    given-names: Keisuke
    affiliation: >-
      NIFE (Niedersächsisches Institut für angewandte Zellgewebezüchtung),
      Leibniz University Hannover / Keio University
    email: kei128608@gmail.com

repository-code: "https://github.com/keisuke58/nife_intern"

url: "https://github.com/keisuke58/nife_intern"

abstract: >-
  Computational pipeline for oral biofilm community dynamics developed
  during the NIFE internship (SIIRI / TRR-298). Connects patient
  metagenomics (MetaPhlAn) to mechanistic COMETS/dFBA simulation and
  fits generalized Lotka–Volterra / Hamilton replicator models with
  metabolic sign priors. Light reproduction via scripts/reproduce_core.sh
  and CI-tested ETL unit tests.

keywords:
  - oral biofilm
  - peri-implantitis
  - generalized Lotka-Volterra
  - COMETS
  - dynamic flux balance analysis
  - metagenomics
  - ecological inference

license: MIT

version: "0.2.0"

date-released: "2026-06-07"